{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:12:54.573Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 1 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Implementation** (all inside scope):\n- `src/watcher/git-guard.ts`: `GitGuard.check()` now returns a `GuardViolation { reason, marker, error }` or `null`. `beginGitGuard` computes a `kill` flag from `vcs.enabled === true` and the pre-spawn HEAD branch starting with `osq/`; only then does `check` return a violation. The `vcs_violation` marker body comes from `formatVcsViolationWarning`, the `scope_violation` body is the files one per line, and `vcs_violation` wins when both happen. Added the new-test-file exemption: an untracked `tests/**` file absent before spawn is not a scope violation.\n- `src/watcher/runner.ts`: stores the guard violation and, after the spawn-failure return, kills with it in one statement. Stays at 197 lines.\n- `src/watcher/failure-reason.ts`: added `vcs_violation` and `scope_violation`.\n- `tests/worktree-guard.test.ts`: new test covering the three \"Violations kill in a worktree\" scenarios, the new-test-file exemption in both worktree and checkout, and both violations at once dying with `vcs_violation`.\n\n**Verification**:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/worktree-guard.test.ts` → 6/6 pass\n- `tests/vcs-guard.test.ts` → 8/8 pass\n- `pnpm typecheck:cli`, `pnpm lint`, line/function/import-graph budgets → pass\n- `pnpm verify` (proposal verify) → passed through lint\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/093-run-in-worktree/.run/results/1.md`."}}
